cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VoxFrontier, please cite it as below."
title: "VoxFrontier: causal and efficiency-frontier analytics for voice-driven livestream performance"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "VoxFrontier contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/GOOD-123-CPU/voxFrontier"
abstract: >-
  An open, fully reproducible research pipeline that quantifies how
  live-streamer voice characteristics relate to streaming efficiency via
  DEA efficiency measurement, exact Shapley attribution, threshold-regime
  modelling, Double Machine Learning causal estimation and counterfactual
  simulation — executed end-to-end on privacy-safe synthetic data.
keywords:
  - DEA
  - Shapley
  - Double Machine Learning
  - threshold regression
  - conformal prediction
  - counterfactual simulation
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-04"
